    "body": "I've been looking at gateway configuration so far, and now that it is web based, it is way less powerful, and I don't know if overriding each of the Form type's and adding the information in the Admin UI is necessarily the right way to go.\r\n\r\nFor example, for Stripe Checkout, I override two main parameters: `payum.template.obtain_token` (to customize look and feel) and `payum.action.convert_payment` (to perform hackery and grab the customer email to auto populate).\r\n\r\nThese parameters don't belong in a UI, in my opinion. They should belong in code, but I just can't see where that could happen in the current configuration.\r\n\r\nEdit: From further testing, where are configuration like `sandbox` for `paypal_express_checkout` set? They are defaulted to `true` in `PaypalExpressCheckoutGatewayFactory`.",
